### Q19. Your manager asks you to configure an alert whenever EC2 CPU utilization goes above 80%. How will you do it?

Spoken answer:

"First, I will open Amazon CloudWatch and navigate to Alarms.

Then I will create a new alarm and select the EC2 CPU Utilization metric.

I will select the required EC2 instance and configure the threshold to 80%.

I will also configure the evaluation period so that the alarm is triggered only when the metric meets the condition for the specified duration.

Finally, I will connect the alarm to an SNS topic so that the administrator receives an email notification when the threshold is breached."

### Q20. Your application is down, but EC2 CPU utilization looks normal. How will you troubleshoot?

Spoken answer:

"CPU utilization alone does not tell us whether an application is healthy.

First, I will check the application and web server logs in CloudWatch.

Then I will verify whether the application process is running and whether the required port is listening.

I will check memory usage, disk space, network connectivity, and database connectivity.

If the application is behind a Load Balancer, I will also check target health and response codes.

This will help me identify whether the issue is related to the application, database, or infrastructure."

# 7. Load Balancer and Auto Scaling Scenarios

