# How to answer scenario-based questions confidently

Use this simple four-step interview formula:

| Step | What to explain |
| --- | --- |
| 1. Identify | What is the actual problem? |
| 2. Investigate | Which AWS service or logs will you check? |
| 3. Resolve | What action will you take? |
| 4. Verify | How will you confirm the issue is fixed? |

For example, if the interviewer asks about an EC2 connectivity issue, don't simply say, "I will check the Security Group."

Instead, explain:

"First, I will check the instance status. Then I will verify Security Groups, NACLs, route tables, and public IP configuration. After identifying the issue, I will correct the configuration and test connectivity again."

This makes your answer sound like someone who has practical troubleshooting knowledge.

